## 3. Seams recorded, nothing edited outside this ticket

1. **Theme tokens (15 rows for the theme owner).** `padel_theme.tres` must grow
   `Palette/colors/*` entries — the screen reads every colour through the palette and records
   any miss in `palette_misses()`:
   `win_green #3fd36f` (`styles.css:2662,2697`), `win_ink #04210f` (`:2697`),
   `loss_red #ff5d7a` (`:2663,2698`), `loss_ink #21040a` (`:2698`),
   `trophy_yellow #ffd23a` (`:2664`), `stat_muted #6f91ad` (`:2655,2704,2717,2722`),
   `item_ink #e6f8ff` (`:2702`), `help_muted #8aa5bc` (`:2437,2623`),
   `kbd_border #29c9dc` (`:1727`), `white #ffffff` (base for the reference's
   `rgba(255,255,255,α)` hairlines/labels: α .03 `:1321`, .05 `:1234`, .55 `:1237`, .72 `:1263`),
   `challenge_cyan #78c8ff` (`:3216,3267`), `challenge_row_fill rgba(8,16,44,.5)` (`:3217`),
   `challenge_done_border rgba(255,210,120,.4)` (`:3222`),
   `challenge_done_fill rgba(60,42,8,.28)` (`:3223`),
   `summary_fill rgba(8,22,48,.6)` (`:3592`).
   **Fulfilled 2026-09-17 (wave 3):** all fifteen rows (plus `stat_bar`/`stat_bar_rival`,
   two inks UIR-11's strip needed) are in `padel_theme.tres`, in `theme/README.md`'s §3
   table with these same sources, and in `theme_probe.gd`'s `PALETTE` map — the three
   places the probe and this log's own audit surface keep in sync. The exact rows, the
   transcription check and the pending engine commands are in
   `uir-wave3-shared-seams.log` §1 and §6–7.
   Already present and used as-is: `ink`, `muted`, `line`, `cyan`, `gold`, `green`,
   `state_yellow_soft`, `tab_border`, `surface_0/1/2`, `text_soft_3`, `shadow`.
2. **Keyboard guide caps are the reference's own groups**, not the input lane's combined
   `KEYBOARD_LEGEND` strings — the label **ids** are asserted equal to
   `input/strings.gd:KEYBOARD_LEGEND[*].label_id` in order, so the two lanes cannot drift.
3. **`tutorial_requested`** is emitted and unbound on the help screen (`SETTINGS.tutorial_link`
   defaults off); UIR-20's pause overlay is the consumer.
4. **Capture harness needs nothing from this lane**: `tests/ui/capture_ui.gd:129-130` reads
   `capture_states()` from the mounted screen, and the router registration is UIR-22's mount.

## 4. Checks actually run (static)

```
$ python3 - <<'PY'  # gdtoolkit is on PATH
$ gdlint godot/src/ui/components/ControlLegend.gd godot/src/ui/screens/HelpScreen.gd \
        godot/src/ui/screens/HistoryScreen.gd godot/src/ui/screens/ChallengesScreen.gd \
        godot/src/ui/screens/ProfileScreen.gd
Success: no problems found
```
Round 1 caught real defects and they were fixed before this log: a C-style ternary (GDScript has
none) in `HistoryScreen`, a `signal` declared after the consts in `ControlLegend`, a duplicated
`load()` of the theme, three lines over the lint length, and two expression-statements that
discarded a call. Nothing in this wave was left half-edited.

## 5. Pending engine work (exact commands — for the engine-owning captain)

```sh
export GODOT=/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot
pgrep -x Godot            # never kill a pre-existing process; wait for an idle window
"$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/screen_help_audit.gd
"$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/screen_history_audit.gd
"$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/screen_challenges_audit.gd
"$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/screen_profile_audit.gd
